    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "fair enough. i guess most people argue that \"targeted reforms\" just end up being more red tape that slows everyone down anyway. like, if you try to regulate everything perfectly, you just kill the growth you were trying to get in the first place. isnt it basically just a choice between a stagnant economy with high safety or a dynamic economy with some risk?",
